<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.paypal.com/us/digital-wallet/manage-money/crypto/pyusd#webpage","name":"PYUSD Stablecoin | US Dollar Crypto Rewards","inLanguage":"us","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://www.paypalobjects.com/marketing/web26/us/pyusd/cat-mm-mkt-global-page-pyusd-component-meta-size-all.jpg#primaryimage","url":"https://www.paypalobjects.com/marketing/web26/us/pyusd/cat-mm-mkt-global-page-pyusd-component-meta-size-all.jpg"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.paypal.com/us/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://www.paypalobjects.com/marketing/web26/us/pyusd/cat-mm-mkt-global-page-pyusd-component-meta-size-all.jpg#primaryimage"}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://www.paypal.com/us/digital-wallet/manage-money/crypto/pyusd#article","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.paypal.com/us/digital-wallet/manage-money/crypto/pyusd#website"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.paypal.com/us/digital-wallet/manage-money/crypto/pyusd#website","image":{"@id":"https://www.paypalobjects.com/marketing/web26/us/pyusd/cat-mm-mkt-global-page-pyusd-component-meta-size-all.jpg#primaryimage"},"headline":"PayPal USD (PYUSD) Stablecoin","description":"PayPal PYUSD Stablecoin is a US dollar cryptocurrency now available to consumers. Learn how to buy it and obtain annual rewards.","publisher":{"@id":"https://www.paypal.com/us/#corporation"}}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a stablecoin?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Stablecoins are a type of cryptocurrency designed to have a steady value over time relative to a reference asset, for example, the U.S. dollar. They can provide inclusive, broad access to the financial system, and can enable fast and efficient money movement. Stablecoins are programmable, offering developers a useful digital currency that can be built into public blockchains and can help link the traditional economy and Web3.\nPayPal USD is a stablecoin that’s backed by US dollar deposits, US treasuries, and similar cash equivalents. You can buy and sell 1 PYUSD for 1 USD on PayPal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is PYUSD available?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PYUSD will soon be available in about 70 markets worldwide, with more countries added over time. You can buy, sell, hold, and earn rewards on PYUSD through your PayPal account in eligible markets across the Americas, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and Africa.\nLearn more: Check your PayPal app to see if PYUSD is available in your country."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I start using PYUSD?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sign in or create a PayPal account, complete identity verification, and opt in to crypto. Then buy PYUSD directly in your PayPal wallet—free with USD, or with a bank account or debit card in eligible regions. Once you have PYUSD, you can send it to friends on or off PayPal, spend it at millions of U.S. merchants where PayPal is accepted, or hold it and opt in to earn 4% PYUSD rewards annually. If you sign up for cryptocurrency services with PayPal, you can buy PYUSD in our app or on our site. Get started."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I find more information about the reserve assets backing PYUSD?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PayPal USD is issued by Paxos Trust Company, LLC (Paxos). PayPal and Paxos are committed to ensuring the public availability of reports on the PayPal USD reserve assets. To that end, Paxos monthly self-reports the composition of the reserve asset portfolio after each month’s end, and monthly attestation reports are also issued by an independent third-party accounting firm. These monthly reports can be found on Paxos’ PayPal USD Transparency page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there fees to use PYUSD?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There are no fees to buy, sell, hold or transfer PYUSD to eligible PayPal users. Conversions to eligible currencies other than USD are subject to an exchange rate, which includes a spread. More about cryptocurrency fees and pricing. Terms apply."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do PYUSD rewards work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PayPal lets you earn rewards for holding PYUSD in your PayPal account. Rewards are calculated using your average daily balance of PYUSD and are paid out monthly in PYUSD. The reward rate is variable. You can view pending rewards within your Crypto hub.\nTo participate, you must:\nBe signed up for crypto\nOpt in to earn rewards\nHold a minimum balance of 1 PYUSD\nYou can also opt out at any time. If you do so, you'll stop accruing new rewards immediately, and any rewards already earned will be paid out on the next scheduled payment date. View terms and conditions.\nIf you withdraw your full PYUSD balance, you'll still receive any rewards earned up to that point on the next payment date.\nPYUSD rewards are coming to more countries.  To check if your country is included, log into your PayPal app, verify your identity, and see if PYUSD is available. Terms apply."}}]}</script>
